---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout title="OnScreenTimer FAQ — Timer, Tasks & Settings" description="Frequently asked questions about OnScreenTimer, including how to use the online timer, manage tasks, use Full mode, and save your session state.">
	<div class="min-h-dvh flex flex-col justify-between">
		<SiteHeader />
		<main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 lg:py-16">
			<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
			
			<div class="space-y-4">
				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900" open>
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						How do I set an online timer?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>First, ensure you have selected Timer mode. Enter your desired duration in the input field using natural formats like <code>5</code>, <code>25mins</code>, or <code>1h 30m</code>. Then press Start.</p>
					</div>
				</details>
				
				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						Do I need an account to use OnScreenTimer?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>No account is required for normal use. It is ready to use immediately without signing up.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						What happens if I refresh the page?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>Your Timer, Stopwatch, tasks, preferences and supported Study Block state may restore when you return or refresh, as they are stored locally in your browser.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						What is Full mode?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>Full mode provides a focused app-level view by hiding nonessential page chrome, keeping only important controls available. It is not the browser Fullscreen API.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						How do Study Block Presets work?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>Choose a preset from Settings. The Timer will use named phases (independent of your Current Task) and progress automatically through each segment until the final one ends.</p>
					</div>
				</details>

				<details class="group border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900">
					<summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer p-4 font-medium text-sm text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-500 rounded-xl">
						Can I use OnScreenTimer as a Pomodoro timer?
						<svg class="w-4 h-4 text-zinc-400 group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform shrink-0 ml-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path></svg>
					</summary>
					<div class="p-4 pt-0 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2">
						<p>Yes, you can manually use it for Pomodoro-style sessions (like 25 minutes work, short break) by setting the timer, or you can use Study Block Presets to follow structured sequences.</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			</div>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</div>
</Layout>
